use std
into extra_test.amni

```amni
import os;
import dm;
import extra;
```

`emit(text const byte[:])` prints text one line at a time with `os::write_stdout`: for each line (split at the newline byte 10, ignoring the empty piece after a final newline) it prints the line followed by a newline, except that an empty line is printed as a single dot "." and a line longer than 100 bytes is printed as its first 20 bytes, a tilde "~" and its length in bytes.

`run(label const byte[:], which int, lang const byte[:], data const byte[:])` calls `dm::dm_reset(kind, unit)` where kind and unit are "ipynb" and "cell" for which 1, "ics" and "event" for 2, "vcf" and "card" for 3, "code" and "line" for 4, then the reader chosen by which: 1 `extra::ex_ipynb(data)`, 2 `extra::ex_ics(data)`, 3 `extra::ex_vcf(data)`, 4 `extra::ex_code(data, lang)`. It prints a line "== " and the label, then the Markdown from `dm::dm_markdown` (written into a scratch list and printed with `emit`), then one line "meta " plus key, an equals sign and value for each line of `dm::dm_meta` (the key and value are separated by the tab byte 9 there), then one line "warn " plus the line for each line of `dm::dm_warn`, and when the reader returned false one line "reader returned false".

`show(name const byte[:], which int)` reads the file "tests/fixtures/" followed by name with `os::read_file` (printing "missing " and the name, and returning, when it cannot be read) and calls `run` with name as the label, which, the text of name after its last period (the whole name when it has none) as lang, and the file's bytes.

`ext_row(list const byte[:])` takes extensions separated by single spaces and prints one line: "ext" followed by, for each extension, a space, the extension, a colon and 1 or 0 for `extra::ex_is_code_ext` of it. An extension written as "_" stands for the empty string (it is still printed as "_").

`main()` calls `show` for these files in this order: "nb4.ipynb", "nb3.ipynb", "nb_edge.ipynb", "nb_empty.ipynb", "nb_trunc.ipynb", "nb_notjson.ipynb" and "nb_other.ipynb", each with 1; "cal.ics", "cal_edge.ics", "cal_empty.ics", "cal_trunc.ics", "cal_bin.ics" and "cal_text.ics", each with 2; "cards.vcf", "cards_edge.vcf", "cards_trunc.vcf", "cards_open.vcf", "cards_bin.vcf" and "cards_text.vcf", each with 3; and then each with 4: "code_src/hello.py", "code_src/lib.rs", "code_src/server.go", "code_src/app.ts", "code_src/app.js", "code_src/util.c", "code_src/Main.java", "code_src/deploy.sh", "code_src/garden.rb", "code_src/tally.he", "code_src/crlf.py", "code_src/longfn.py", "code_src/flat.py", "code_src/longsig.rs" and "code_src/bin.c". Then it calls `run("inline c1", 4, ".PY", "x = 1\n")`, `run("inline c2", 4, "weird", "alpha\nbeta\n")`, `run("inline c3", 4, "py", "")`, `run("inline c4", 4, "go", "func a() {\n}\n\nfunc b() {\n}")` and `run("inline c5", 4, "py", "def a():\n    return 1\n\n\n\n\n")`, then `ext_row("py PY .rs Dockerfile mk make txt md _ . pyc c++ kts scss vhd toml json gold he amni ..py cs fs v")`, and lastly `run("inline empty ics", 2, "", "")`, `run("inline empty vcf", 3, "", "")` and `run("inline empty nb", 1, "", "")`.

